WEBVTT

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:17.030
<i>Negotiator Tsukai Saraka opened up 
to Shindo Kojiro about her feelings.</i>

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:22.160
<i>Saraka's desire to protect the 
dignity of humanity and this world</i>

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.720
<i>sent ripples through the 
still pond of Shindo's mind.</i>

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.880
<i>However, Gonno Takumi, 
who is now working for SETTEN,</i>

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.720
<i>and the company CEO, Adam Ward,</i>

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.970
<i>decided to broadcast footage of the 
anisotropic device, the Sansa, to the world.</i>

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.990
This broadcast will contain footage of a special device given to us by the anisotropic. 
<b>Viewing this device may have unexpected effects on the human body.</b>
Please keep this in mind if you wish to continue viewing.

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:42.430
<i>Yaha-kui zaShunina made a live appearance</i>

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:41.380
<b>Emergency Press Conference by Yaha-kui zaShunina, the anisotropic being 
After this, a new device separate from the Wam will be revealed</b>

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.380
A Message from the Anisotropic to Humanity
<b>The new device's name is "Sansa"</b>

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.000
<i>and revealed the Sansa to the world.</i>

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:48.190
<i>The world continues to accelerate.</i>

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.160
Nanomis-hein

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:31.830
They're going inside.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.380
Hanamori-san, can you contact Shindo-san?

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.890
We can't contact anyone inside Kado.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.980
I think if we yell for him outside, though,

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:45.470
zaShunina will open it up.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.080
Is that not good enough?

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:51.470
I have a bad feeling, for some reason...

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.590
Kado.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.750
Enter, Shindo.

00:03:19.430 --> 00:03:21.320
I've been thinking...

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.190
Can't you make this thing 
a little easier to use?

00:03:25.150 --> 00:03:26.970
Like make it a door, or a tunnel?

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:30.250
No.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.270
What was that pause for?

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:37.070
Well, there's no point in complaining 
about the things you do at this point.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:50.750
What is this place?

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.280
Kado is a boundary object, 
and deep inside it

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.360
is the split between the universe
and the anisotropic.

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:01.340
This point is approximately 
equidistant to both of them.

00:04:10.380 --> 00:04:12.780
Everything you do is so sudden...

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:18.080
It's probably too late to be asking,

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.560
but can you drink?

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.540
This is the first time.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.610
I've been interested in it, though.

00:04:29.320 --> 00:04:30.540
Cheers.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.510
Well?

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:42.700
It's bitter.

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:48.470
Now, then...

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:50.630
The Sansa was revealed to the world.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:56.230
Just like with the Wam, the world will 
likely go forward at an incredible rate.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:59.270
The old culture will change drastically.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.780
What was inconvenient will become convenient,

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.270
and what was impossible will become possible.

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:11.660
But some humans see this 
change as destruction.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:17.040
What are your thoughts on this acceleration?

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:19.590
Shindo.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.990
There's something I want you to see today.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:24.620
Kado.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.170
When I came to this universe,

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:32.980
I prepared four things.

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:34.890
Kado.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:40.230
The Wam.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:45.890
The Sansa.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.090
And...

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.280
The fourth.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.750
Nanomis-hein.

00:06:06.310 --> 00:06:08.970
Mifune-sensei, what is that?

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:11.740
When Shinawa saw the Sansa,

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:14.970
she started to work on her calculations 
like a woman possessed.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.730
And then she started saying 
she wanted to see Fregonics.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.090
Yes, yes, yes, this, this, this!

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:32.500
Did she come up with some new insight?

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.700
I try to learn this this stuff, and I can't...

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:35.890
I think with the neuron layout 
at this dimensional level,

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.920
She's capable of perfectly creating the Wam.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:37.890
the information doesn't 
get properly signified.

00:06:36.920 --> 00:06:38.610
So it's possible that

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:39.900
But the signifiés are 
being properly captured,

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:43.710
seeing the Sansa has moved her 
to levels that we can't yet reach.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.400
so we can do it if we just develop the 
signifiants on our own. Yeah, that'll work.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.730
It's front and back, so 
maybe bront and frack?

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:44.840
Dr. Shinawa!

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:47.730
Dr. Shinawa!

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:50.840
At Haneda Airport, you were 
working on research

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:54.480
that would allow you to interfere 
with the Fregonics, right?

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.730
I sure was!

00:06:55.730 --> 00:06:57.560
I failed, though.

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:01.510
After interacting with the Wam and Sansa,

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:04.110
you've gained a new sense of the anisotropic.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:09.240
Do you think you could come up with a 
way to interfere with Fregonics now?

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:27.470
It's definitely higher energy than 
the bulk that's not surface-level.

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:29.420
It has more axes than membranes, 
so would that work?

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.330
But that wouldn't stick!

00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:32.230
You'd need friction first! 
A vertical surface!

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:33.470
No, there's nothing under it...

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:37.350
Shindo, begin by touching it.

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:00.660
Did you feel arms?

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:03.450
Yeah...

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:08.420
The Nanomis-hein is more broadly 
usable than the Wam or Sansa.

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:10.670
I'll show you one such application.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:18.350
Take it.

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:37.140
It's light...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.830
There's no weight to it.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:58.010
I'll translate this phenomenon

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.320
into an expression that is 
short and simple to understand.

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:03.680
Gravitational control.

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:05.830
Inertial control.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:08.360
Mass control.

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:10.660
The control of all of these.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:17.570
The Nanomis-hein is a device that can aid 
humanity's control of the anisotropic.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:21.120
You could call it the arm 
of an anisotropic being.

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:22.610
The arm...

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:25.120
In the time between Kado's 
appearance and today,

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:29.460
you and others have seen various 
methods of anisotropic control.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:33.920
The Nanomis-hein makes it 
possible for this control

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.930
to be performed within the universe.

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:40.930
Can you imagine what this means?

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.030
Yeah, I can.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:45.320
Innovation in commodity distribution.

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.450
A revolution in transportation.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.000
Space exploration.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.250
The possibilities are infinite.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:54.790
The very concept of "work" will change.

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:58.700
Everything will be made 
vastly more efficient.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:05.220
This goes far beyond economic effects.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:09.690
A blind race toward the 
future is about to begin.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:12.530
An entire age, gripped by a fever.

00:10:12.980 --> 00:10:15.590
A bubble period for all of humanity.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:17.590
That's not quite correct.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.260
Assuming a level of

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:24.110
production that produces more goods than 
could ever be consumed in the future,

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:28.210
and yet continuing to operate an 
economy is the definition of a bubble.

00:10:28.810 --> 00:10:31.900
Put another way, you "create too much."

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:33.680
Isn't that what would result from this?

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:35.380
No, that's not right.

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:40.700
Humanity's production will 
never exceed its consumption.

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:45.200
Not for the rest of eternity.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.750
How can you be so sure?

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.660
Because they will have the anisotropic.

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:14.010
I've increased its mass.

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:16.470
It's impossible for a single
person to move it.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.690
Wow...

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.660
It's definitely possible, though.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:26.550
If you can exchange energy from the 
universe with the anisotropic via the Wam,

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:30.660
it would make sense if you could break the 
law of conservation of angular momentum.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:33.250
That's also incorrect, Shindo.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:39.800
The Nanomis-hein does not exchange momentum 
between the universe and the anisotropic.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.970
Then how does it work?

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:44.220
To explain the principles behind it,

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:47.640
we need to go back to our root.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:48.670
Root?

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:50.930
The anisotropic.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:52.960
That's the central issue, isn't it?

00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.840
It will be a long talk.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:56.680
Will you listen, Shindo?

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:58.650
That's why I'm here.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.870
Let's take a walk.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.760
That surprised me back there.

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:29.890
You want to do something 
about the Fregonics?

00:12:29.890 --> 00:12:32.430
zaShunina isn't answering.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:35.270
I want to do everything I can,

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.400
just in case the worst-case scenario happens.

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.610
Are you in love with Shindo-san?

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:45.200
I heard you took him to meet your parents.

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.510
That's not true!

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:47.850
It's not!

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:50.620
You don't need to try so hard to deny it.

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:54.000
I love him, too.

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:59.850
Natsume-san likes him, too.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:01.300
D-Does she?

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:06.380
I asked her once if she liked him, and...

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.430
I do.

00:13:15.220 --> 00:13:19.150
I don't think I'm the person for him, though.

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:20.940
What do you mean?

00:13:21.710 --> 00:13:24.360
I'm not capable of handling him.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.870
I'm sure the person for him

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.380
is someone far greater.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:39.340
Anyway, it looks like
Natsume-san won't go for it,

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.600
so this is your chance!

00:13:40.600 --> 00:13:42.840
I told you, I'm not...

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.130
Wait, are you dating someone, though?

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:48.640
I mean, that.

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:52.390
I'm not seeing anyone.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:54.060
Is it just for fashion?

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:56.490
This is...

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.910
A pledge of faith.

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:08.760
You once described the anisotropic as 
a higher dimensional world, didn't you?

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:09.530
Yes.

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:12.330
I corrected you because 
it wasn't quite correct,

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:14.520
but in the larger sense, it is correct.

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:19.550
The number of dimensions is a concise 
parameter of an amount of information.

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:21.610
One dimension.

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:23.990
Two dimensions.

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:26.900
Three dimensions.

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:32.840
Now, Shindo.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.680
Let's say that a single 
one of these is one bit,

00:14:35.680 --> 00:14:38.330
and that this cluster of them is a CPU.

00:14:39.450 --> 00:14:41.100
Can you comprehend this?

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:44.380
As the number of dimensions increases, 
the number of bits increases,

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:46.580
and the processing power increases rapidly.

00:14:47.450 --> 00:14:48.520
Indeed.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.280
The number of dimensions in the anisotropic

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:53.830
would add 37 to this universe.

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.140
Each increase in dimensions results in

00:14:58.140 --> 00:15:00.450
exponential growth in
the information contained.

00:15:01.560 --> 00:15:04.590
A world where size and processing speed are

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:07.300
increased to the 37th power 
beyond that of this universe.

00:15:08.140 --> 00:15:09.900
That is the anisotropic.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:18.830
But Shindo, the needs of this vast 
world aren't completely fulfilled.

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:24.180
The vast processing power of 
the anisotropic can process

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:27.060
any information in an instant.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:31.490
Therefore, it is plagued by 
a constant lack of information.

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:34.120
"We want information.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.030
We want to absorb a huge 
amount of information.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:43.040
We want to bathe in more information 
than we could ever process."

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:46.670
And for that purpose,

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:51.310
the anisotropic beings created 
"the information cocoon."

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:59.430
What are your thoughts on the Wam 
and Sansa, Mifune-sensei?

00:15:59.800 --> 00:16:01.440
In what sense?

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:05.630
In other words, are they really a good thing?

00:16:07.580 --> 00:16:10.660
The Wam and Sansa are neither 
good nor evil in themselves.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:15.070
Another standard is required 
to judge what they are.

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:17.580
Another standard?

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:20.690
By our standard, it's simple.

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:26.200
Anything that contributes to the survival 
and happiness of humanity is good.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:32.740
The problem is what happens when another 
standard besides humanity's exists.

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:37.030
The information cocoon?

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:40.210
You have a concept called 
"sericulture," do you not?

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:44.200
You raise silkworms and take 
threads from their cocoons.

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:47.750
Just think of us as taking 
information instead of threads.

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:51.910
The anisotropic beings 
made countless cocoons.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.400
We changed their initial conditions,

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.330
observed their growth,

00:16:56.950 --> 00:17:00.110
and waited for high-density information 
to be born from the cocoons.

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:03.160
We waited for an eternity,

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:08.250
and at last, the ultimate thread was born.

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:12.500
That thread was the first 
miraculous body of information

00:17:12.500 --> 00:17:14.630
that the anisotropic beings met.

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:22.310
A thing that created vast 
information under its own power.

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:23.810
A singularity.

00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:28.010
It was a gospel that would bring 
happiness to the anisotropic.

00:17:29.390 --> 00:17:31.610
And that thread was...

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:37.220
Humanity.

00:17:39.770 --> 00:17:42.040
The information cocoon is a universe.

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:45.540
The ultimate thread is humanity.

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.480
It was the anisotropic beings 
that created this universe.

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.150
We opened the space and 
decided the initial values,

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:55.880
as well as some of its natural parameters.

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:58.180
The speed of light...

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:00.300
The units of force...

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:04.810
All were decided by the anisotropic beings?

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:06.510
Shall I show you?

00:18:14.670 --> 00:18:16.300
Hey, zaShunina!

00:18:16.300 --> 00:18:16.820
Hey!

00:18:19.050 --> 00:18:21.490
The alteration of temporal 
values within an area.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:24.640
It's not an exchange of 
momentum with the anisotropic.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:29.120
The Nanomis-hein is the arm of the 
anisotropic, which allows you to alter

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.770
the settings of the universe.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:37.590
Oh, I see.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.590
I'm sorry, Shindo.

00:18:44.990 --> 00:18:47.850
I tried temporarily altering 
our relative times.

00:18:48.740 --> 00:18:55.230
What was 10 seconds to me 
was about 70 hours to you.

00:18:57.640 --> 00:19:00.990
Are you... God?

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:05.210
A complete mistake.

00:19:05.990 --> 00:19:08.330
I am merely an anisotropic being.

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:11.670
If you wish to use the expression "God,"

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:15.920
the true divine miracle is you, humanity.

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:22.720
Shindo.

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:29.640
Will you come with me to the anisotropic?

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:55.040
zaShunina.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:19:59.590
It was too soon, then?

00:20:01.090 --> 00:20:02.550
It's done!

00:20:02.550 --> 00:20:05.100
Shinawa-san, what happened to the Fregonics?

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.920
I can interfere with them.

00:20:06.920 --> 00:20:09.260
I bet I could break them, too.

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:12.260
I see! It's the other side of this?

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:13.810
So, what do we do?

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.120
What?

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.590
I want to go to the other side.

00:20:16.590 --> 00:20:17.550
Now!

00:20:18.140 --> 00:20:20.070
I don't know about that...

00:20:20.070 --> 00:20:22.290
No, I can't do it right away.

00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:24.180
I just figured out that I <i>can</i> break it.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.620
I need extra calculations, plus I'd need

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:26.840
to make some kind of device.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:29.950
I can't just rip through it with my 
hands like an anisotropic being!

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:31.970
Isn't there something you can do?

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:33.240
Not a thing.

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.710
You're looking at three days, minimum.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:41.840
Kado.

00:20:45.660 --> 00:20:46.930
Shindo,

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:52.740
what I told you today was another effort 
to advance humanity and the universe.

00:20:53.540 --> 00:20:56.620
I wanted you to properly 
understand the anisotropic

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:59.660
and come with me to the next stage.

00:21:00.820 --> 00:21:03.860
However, it seems it was too soon.

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:10.670
This is a copy of you several 
hours ago, created by Kado.

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:14.940
I want to start over with this one.

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:24.710
And as for you,

00:21:25.310 --> 00:21:26.530
I want you to disappear.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:40.710
I see.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:47.630
So you're the administrator of this cocoon.

00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:55.500
Anisotropic being...

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:58.990
Tsukai Saraka.

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:37.310
Saraka-san!

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:41.190
I possess all of the anisotropic. 
You cannot fight me.

00:23:41.190 --> 00:23:44.310
If you do that, humanity will be broken!

00:23:44.310 --> 00:23:47.280
Tell me! What is the right answer?

00:23:47.280 --> 00:23:49.450
Shindo, this is goodbye.

00:23:48.630 --> 00:23:52.000
Towanosakiwa'
